  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given NNN students standing in a row, each student iii has an **distinct** achievement score AiA_iAi​ provided in an array A=[A1,A2,…,An]A = [A_1, A_2, \\dots, A_n]A=[A1​,A2​,…,An​]. The array AAA consists of distinct integers from 111 to NNN.\n\nA student iii ( 1≤i≤N1 \\leq i \\leq N1≤i≤N ) will be happy if their achievement score AiA_iAi​ is greater than the achievement scores of all the students standing before them in the array.\n\nThe task is to print whether a student is happy or not.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains NNN — the number of students.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​, denoting the achievement scores of the students.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\n\n\nFor each test case, print a single line containing NNN integers. Print ithi^{th}ith integer as 111 if the ithi^{th}ith student is happy, otherwise print 000.\n\n\n\n\nEach test case's output should be on a new line, with the integers separated by spaces.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤4×1051 \\leq T \\leq 4 \\times 10^51≤T≤4×105",
      "1≤N≤101 \\leq N \\leq 101≤N≤10",
      "1≤Ai≤N1 \\leq A_i \\leq N1≤Ai​≤N",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 4×1054 \\times 10^54×105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n5\n3 1 2 4 5\n4\n1 2 3 4",
        "output": "1 0 0 1 1\n1 1 1 1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1:\n\nThere is no student behind student 111, so he is happy.\nFor student 222, there is student 111 with greater achievement score, so he is not happy.\nSimilarly for student 333, there is student 111 with greater score, so he is not happy.\nStudent 444 has greater achievement score than student 111, student 222, and student 333, so student 444 is happy.\nStudent 555 has greater score than all other students, so he is happy."
      }
    ]
  },
